NoJIT for WoW64: run only code from the AOT image (FEX 3bec2ac, on top of 0011)

Port of patches/fex/0008 to Madeira's FEX fork. On iOS without a debugger
attached, memory can never be made executable. With NoJIT=1 FEX does not
ask for it:

- JIT code buffers are allocated read+write only; nothing runs from them.
- ContextImpl::CompileBlock stops FEX with an error naming the guest block
  when a block is not in the lookup cache, i.e. not in the AOT image,
  instead of compiling it.
- The dispatcher must come from the AOT image (patch 0011). If the index
  has no dispatcher entry, or its copy does not match this build, FEX stops
  instead of making its own dispatcher executable. Otherwise it logs
  "[nojit] no code is generated to run".

